      "stageRecord": "On the ordinary impersonal reading, the sentence means that people in general live well here. Vivir is intransitive: its external argument is the silent arbitrary-human subject in the specifier of IP, and it selects no object. This analysis uses the classical GB placement of the external argument in Spec-IP rather than a VP-internal subject position. The verb assigns that subject its external theta-role. Bien is a manner adjunct to VP; aquí is a second, outer VP adjunct locating the living situation. Neither adverb is a selected argument. The abstract finite I bears present-tense, third-person singular features. Se is initially a separate clitic awaiting attachment to the finite head; its arbitrary-subject licensing relation is not yet established. The lexical terminal vive already has its supplied whole-word form, so the abstract inflectional head does not introduce a separately pronounced suffix.",
