      "stageRecord": "Vive raises from the previously displayed V position to finite I, leaving a silent head trace. The raised verb locally binds and antecedent-governs that trace, satisfying the ECP for the head-movement chain. Se then attaches on the left of the resulting finite head, producing the order Se vive without changing either terminal's whole-word realization. The impersonal clitic identifies the silent subject as arbitrary human, while finite I formally licenses pro and assigns it nominative Case. Third-person singular is the impersonal agreement form, not agreement with a covert plural noun phrase. Se is a nonargumental impersonal clitic in this analysis, not a referential reflexive NP, so it does not introduce a Principle A anaphor or an additional theta-role. Finally, a silent declarative C takes the completed IP as its complement. The resulting tree accounts for all four input tokens and retains the manner and locative adjuncts in their established positions.",
